This displays the operational mode for each profile (Domain, Private, Public): 
whether inbound and outbound connections are allowed by default, whether the firewall is on or off, and whether stateful inspection is enabled.

netsh advfirewall show allprofiles


netsh advfirewall set allprofiles state on


Check the active profile for the interface experiencing the issue:

netsh advfirewall show currentprofile

Get-NetConnectionProfile | Select Name, InterfaceAlias, NetworkCategory



If the profile is misclassified (for example, a corporate domain network stuck in Public), 
inbound services will be blocked regardless of rules. Fix this with:

Set-NetConnectionProfile -InterfaceAlias "Ethernet" -NetworkCategory DomainAuthenticated


Set Wi-Fi to Private:
Set-NetConnectionProfile -InterfaceAlias "Wi-Fi" -NetworkCategory Private

Set Wi-Fi to Public:
Set-NetConnectionProfile -InterfaceAlias "Wi-Fi" -NetworkCategory Public


