Press Win + R to open the Run dialog

gpedit.msc

Expand Administrative Templates

Expand Network

Expand Network Connections

- Domain Profile: Settings that kick in when your machine is connected to a corporate Active Directory domain.
- Standard Profile: Settings that apply when you are on a Private or Public home/work network.

Double-clicking any policy (like "Windows Defender Firewall: Protect all network connections"). A window opens showing three main choices

- Not Configured: Windows defaults to its local settings (default).
- Enabled: Forces the policy ON.
- Disabled: Forces the policy OFF.

